  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs` `mod[tests]/impl[Project/Domain]/fn[node_path]` is a valid function-level coverage exception.\n\n- **Form:** the citation is a fenced `:::{cite} habeas:coverage` block on an explicit function with a body. Its commentary gives a substantive reason: this is a required `Domain` trait method that the source-tool flows never call.\n- **Callers:** a search for `node_path` finds callers outside test fixtures only in `agent/tools.rs` and in `graph.rs`. The `agent/tools.rs` callers are `GraphSession` code: `ToolAgent::run`, `GraphSession::node` and `GraphSession::dispatch`. The `graph.rs` callers are `edge_fingerprint`, reached via `dependencies_are_current` and `prepare_edges`, so only through outgoing-edge handling. The `Project` fixture drives none of these paths.\n- **Source-tool tests:** the `Project` tests use `ProjectSources` sessions through `SessionTools`. In `fixed_tools_deliver_domain_contents_with_mandatory_snapshot_dependencies`, `read_source` records `Dependency::Node(\"source-node\", …)`. That is a mapped `NodeId`, held directly in dependencies, and no path conversion is involved. `OutlineId` addresses are published as `path` and `selector`.\n- **Validator test:** `source_capable_validator_tracks_deterministic_reads_and_reuses_saved_results` is the same. `ReadSource::execute` calls `cx.read_source(&OutlineId{…})` and never calls `node_path`.\n- **Edges:** `Project::outgoing_edges` returns an empty list, so `edge_fingerprint` has nothing to convert.\n- **Storage:** `Project::load_evidence` and `Project::store_evidence` ignore the node and use the stored record, so they never convert it to a path.\n- **Other domains:** tests for stable paths and filesystem storage use other domains, as the commentary says. These are `StoredGraph` in `tests/storage.rs`, and `Application` and `Relationships` in `tests/contracts.rs`.\n\nThe explanation therefore agrees with the current source. The citation is a coverage exception rather than an {impl} or {test} claim, so it is not redundant.",
